<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Key Benefits of This App=
roach:</strong></p>
<ol class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Zero Ejection Risk</str=
ong>: All modifications are external to CRA core</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Gradual Migration</stro=
ng>: Can enable compiler component by component</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Easy Rollback</strong>:=
 Simple to disable or remove configurations</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Monitoring Integration<=
/strong>: Full visibility into compilation effectiveness</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Team Familiarity</stron=
g>: Maintains existing CRA development workflows</li>
</ol>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Risk Mitigation for Busi=
ness-Critical Applications:</strong></p>
<ol class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Feature Flags</strong>:=
 Use environment variables to enable/disable compiler</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>A/B Testing</strong>: S=
plit traffic between compiled and non-compiled versions</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Comprehensive Testing</=
strong>: Both unit and integration tests for all migration scenarios</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Performance Monitoring<=
/strong>: Real-time tracking of build and runtime performance</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Fallback Procedures</st=
rong>: Documented rollback steps with maximum 15-minute recovery time</li>
</ol>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">This approach ensures that <stro=
ng>business-critical CRA applications can benefit from React Compiler</stro=
ng> without the risks associated with ejection or major architectural chang=
es.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Interviewer</strong>: Ex=
cellent! Your CRA strategy is particularly impressive - the selective compi=
lation approach and micro-frontend fallback show real-world pragmatism. Now=
 let's talk about the operational side. Once you have React Compiler instal=
led across these diverse applications, how would you verify that it's actua=
lly working correctly? The documentation mentions checking React DevTools a=
nd build output, but at enterprise scale with dozens of applications, how w=
ould you automate this verification and ongoing monitoring?</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Candidate</strong>: <str=
